{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "03608",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.64,
      "end_seconds": 3.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "Hello, come in. Mind the step."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 4.18,
      "end_seconds": 8.32,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "Thank you for fitting us in, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 9.39,
      "end_seconds": 15.72,
      "duration_seconds": 6.33,
      "text": "Please do. Extra information is always welcome. So what can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 17.5,
      "end_seconds": 22.85,
      "duration_seconds": 5.35,
      "text": "Ah, I've been dealing with being a bit constipated."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.37,
      "end_seconds": 29.33,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "Did it come on recently?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 30.39,
      "end_seconds": 45.37,
      "duration_seconds": 14.98,
      "text": "Uh, probably one week. Yeah. I'm hoping you can tell me something definite. A neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 45.89,
      "end_seconds": 52.67,
      "duration_seconds": 6.78,
      "text": "I, I was just going to say that the main thing is—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 52.77,
      "end_seconds": 60.06,
      "duration_seconds": 7.29,
      "text": "Sorry to cut in, doctor, quick question: shall I bring the trolley in now or later?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 61.54,
      "end_seconds": 68.47,
      "duration_seconds": 6.93,
      "text": "Later, thanks. Please go on. Alright, has there been a vague tummy ache too?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 69.13,
      "end_seconds": 73.18,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "Yeah, I've had that since last night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 74.7,
      "end_seconds": 77.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "How much trouble does it give you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 79.09,
      "end_seconds": 80.41,
      "duration_seconds": 1.32,
      "text": "Mild, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 82.3,
      "end_seconds": 88.46,
      "duration_seconds": 6.16,
      "text": "Alright, have you had being a bit constipated before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.47,
      "end_seconds": 98.27,
      "duration_seconds": 8.8,
      "text": "Let me think, a bit, a couple of years ago. It settled by itself back then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.33,
      "end_seconds": 107.32,
      "duration_seconds": 6.99,
      "text": "Have you had any high fever, blood in the stool, urinary symptoms or vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.95,
      "end_seconds": 126.05,
      "duration_seconds": 18.1,
      "text": "No, uh, no high fever, no blood in the stool, no urinary symptoms. I did have poor appetite for two days at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 127.69,
      "end_seconds": 129.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "Anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 131.92,
      "end_seconds": 133.73,
      "duration_seconds": 1.81,
      "text": "No changes there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 134.89,
      "end_seconds": 138.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.73,
      "text": "Anything on the skin I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 139.48,
      "end_seconds": 143.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.77,
      "text": "Actually, nothing on the skin, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 144.56,
      "end_seconds": 146.4,
      "duration_seconds": 1.84,
      "text": "Have you retired yet?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 149.54,
      "end_seconds": 154.22,
      "duration_seconds": 4.68,
      "text": "I retired from the post office two years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 167.92,
      "end_seconds": 170.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Have you been to theatre before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 171.15,
      "end_seconds": 177.23,
      "duration_seconds": 6.08,
      "text": "I had a meniscus repair on my knee four years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 177.85,
      "end_seconds": 181.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "Has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 182.2,
      "end_seconds": 190.86,
      "duration_seconds": 8.66,
      "text": "Erm, I have high blood pressure. Work has been very busy so I kept ignoring it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.45,
      "end_seconds": 194.0,
      "duration_seconds": 1.55,
      "text": "Is there anything more?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 194.81,
      "end_seconds": 196.46,
      "duration_seconds": 1.65,
      "text": "Yes, heart failure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 197.49,
      "end_seconds": 199.28,
      "duration_seconds": 1.79,
      "text": "Is there anything more?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 200.42,
      "end_seconds": 204.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "I've had eczema for about a year now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 205.77,
      "end_seconds": 215.39,
      "duration_seconds": 9.62,
      "text": "Right, so heart failure is already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today. Is there anything relevant on the family side?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 217.18,
      "end_seconds": 223.14,
      "duration_seconds": 5.96,
      "text": "My sister had breast cancer. My uncle has high cholesterol."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 234.05,
      "end_seconds": 238.14,
      "duration_seconds": 4.09,
      "text": "Are you taking anything regularly, including from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 238.64,
      "end_seconds": 243.84,
      "duration_seconds": 5.2,
      "text": "He takes furosemide, 40 milligrams, every morning for the fluid."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 245.28,
      "end_seconds": 253.86,
      "duration_seconds": 8.58,
      "text": "I had hydrocortisone cream at one point, you know, but I'm off it now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 257.44,
      "end_seconds": 269.17,
      "duration_seconds": 11.73,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. BMI works out to 23.0, pressure 116 over 72, temp 36.9 degrees. Pulse 77, weight 68 kilos, height 172 centimetres."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.69,
      "end_seconds": 271.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "So, good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 273.49,
      "end_seconds": 276.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.6,
      "text": "Let's move on to the examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 277.97,
      "end_seconds": 279.43,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "Fine by me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.88,
      "end_seconds": 284.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.33,
      "text": "Stay as you are for a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 292.8,
      "end_seconds": 302.73,
      "duration_seconds": 9.93,
      "text": "Your tummy is soft but tender low on the right with mild guarding, and the temperature is only a little up."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 307.24,
      "end_seconds": 319.75,
      "duration_seconds": 12.51,
      "text": "You can relax now. From what you've told me and what I found, this is probably possible appendicitis, which can look mild in older people. I'd also keep diverticulitis in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 321.23,
      "end_seconds": 325.52,
      "duration_seconds": 4.29,
      "text": "I'm scared it's something bad. Is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 327.43,
      "end_seconds": 352.15,
      "duration_seconds": 24.72,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like possible appendicitis, which can look mild in older people, but I'd like to confirm. Let me just check I've got this right. You've had being a bit constipated for one week, and no high fever or blood in the stool."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 352.93,
      "end_seconds": 355.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "Yes, you've got it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 357.02,
      "end_seconds": 374.76,
      "duration_seconds": 17.74,
      "text": "A CT scan of the abdomen is what I'd like next, for right iliac fossa tenderness. Blood tests is what I'd like next, for abdominal pain. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 376.83,
      "end_seconds": 378.29,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "Does it hurt?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 380.09,
      "end_seconds": 397.49,
      "duration_seconds": 17.4,
      "text": "Even though you look fairly well, I'd like the surgeons to see you today. I'm going to send a referral to the surgical team. Let's plan a check straight away. I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 399.37,
      "end_seconds": 405.18,
      "duration_seconds": 5.81,
      "text": "Um, uh, great, thank you for your help."
    }
  ]
}